 "verdict_reason": "There is no hostile attacker. A governance upgrade of the bridge proxy (tx 0x855dd3b1..., 08:48:47) left withdrawals checked in a way that let a modified receipt pass; the first post-upgrade user withdrawals became bot bait. Three independent searchers each saw a legitimate user withdrawal (receipt ids 166631-166633) in the public mempool and sent a copy with the recipient (and for two of them the quantity) rewritten, ahead of it: ETH leg 0x26195700 (block 20468679 pos 0, 3,996.09375 ETH), a third racer 0x77bb83dd (block 20468790 pos 0, 2.4173 ETH, quantity unchanged) and Yoink 0xbce5b854 (block 20468848 pos 1, 1,998,046.875 USDC). Calldata diffs: ETH leg differs from the user's tx in 2 of 76 words, racer 3 in 1 of 67, Yoink in 3 of 61. All three were placed ahead of the user's tx, which stayed pending and later reverted.",
